🚀 Top 10 Spring Boot Deployment Configurations for Kubernetes & AWS ECS

Senior Java Developer Interview Revision Sheet
☸️ Kubernetes Deployment Configurations
1. Deployment

Purpose: Deploy and manage Spring Boot Pods.

apiVersion: apps/v1

kind: Deployment

metadata:
  name: springboot-app

spec:
  replicas: 2


✅ Features:

Creates Pods
Self Healing
Rolling Updates
Scaling
2. Service

Purpose: Expose Spring Boot application inside/outside the cluster.

apiVersion: v1

kind: Service

spec:
  selector:
    app: springboot-app

  ports:
    - port: 80
      targetPort: 8080

Flow
Client
  ↓
Service
  ↓
Pods

3. ConfigMap

Purpose: Store environment-specific configuration.

envFrom:
  - configMapRef:
      name: app-config

Examples
Database URL
API URLs
Feature Flags

❌ Not for passwords

4. Secret

Purpose: Store sensitive configuration.

env:
  - name: DB_PASSWORD
    valueFrom:
      secretKeyRef:
        name: db-secret
        key: password

Examples
Passwords
API Keys
Certificates
JWT Secrets
5. Resource Requests & Limits

Purpose: Prevent resource starvation.

resources:
  requests:
    cpu: "200m"
    memory: "512Mi"

  limits:
    cpu: "500m"
    memory: "1Gi"

Interview Answer
Requests = Minimum guaranteed resources

Limits = Maximum permitted resources

6. Readiness Probe

Purpose: Checks whether application can serve traffic.

readinessProbe:
  httpGet:
    path: /actuator/health/readiness
    port: 8080

If Probe Fails
Pod remains running

Traffic is stopped

7. Liveness Probe

Purpose: Checks whether application is alive.

livenessProbe:
  httpGet:
    path: /actuator/health/liveness
    port: 8080

If Probe Fails
Pod restarted automatically

8. Ingress

Purpose: Expose application through URL.

apiVersion: networking.k8s.io/v1

kind: Ingress

spec:
  rules:
    - host: api.bank.com

Flow
Internet
   ↓
Ingress
   ↓
Service
   ↓
Pods

9. Horizontal Pod Autoscaler (HPA)

Purpose: Auto-scale Pods.

apiVersion: autoscaling/v2

kind: HorizontalPodAutoscaler

spec:
  minReplicas: 2
  maxReplicas: 10

Example
CPU > 70%

2 Pods
   ↓
10 Pods

10. Persistent Volume Claim (PVC)

Purpose: Persistent Storage.

volumes:
  - name: app-storage

    persistentVolumeClaim:
      claimName: app-pvc

Used For
Logs
Files
Uploads
🏆 Most Asked Full Kubernetes Deployment YAML
apiVersion: apps/v1

kind: Deployment

metadata:
  name: springboot-app

spec:
  replicas: 2

  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: springboot-app

  template:

    metadata:
      labels:
        app: springboot-app

    spec:

      containers:

        - name: springboot-app

          image: myrepo/springboot:1.0

          ports:
            - containerPort: 8080

          envFrom:
            - configMapRef:
                name: app-config

          readinessProbe:
            httpGet:
              path: /actuator/health/readiness
              port: 8080

          livenessProbe:
            httpGet:
              path: /actuator/health/liveness
              port: 8080

          resources:
            requests:
              cpu: "200m"
              memory: "512Mi"

            limits:
              cpu: "500m"
              memory: "1Gi"

☁️ AWS ECS Deployment Configurations
1. ECS Cluster

Purpose: Logical group of ECS Services.

ECS Cluster
├── Payment Service
├── Customer Service
└── Notification Service

2. ECS Service

Purpose: Maintains desired number of Tasks.

Desired Count = 2

If one Task crashes:
  ↓
Automatically recreated

3. ECS Task Definition

Purpose: Blueprint of container.

Contains
Docker Image
CPU
Memory
Ports
Environment Variables
IAM Roles
4. ECS Execution Role

Used By: ECS Runtime

Allows
Pull Images from ECR
Send Logs to CloudWatch
5. ECS Task Role

Used By: Application

Allows Access To
S3
SNS
SQS
Secrets Manager
Parameter Store
6. Amazon ECR

Purpose: Docker Image Repository

docker build -t springboot-app .

docker push <ecr-url>

7. Application Load Balancer (ALB)

Purpose: Routes traffic to healthy tasks.

Flow
User
 ↓
ALB
 ↓
ECS Tasks

Supports
SSL
Path Routing
Health Checks
8. CloudWatch Logs

Purpose: Centralized Logging

Spring Boot Logs
        ↓
CloudWatch

Sample Configuration
{
  "logConfiguration": {
    "logDriver": "awslogs"
  }
}

9. Secrets Manager

Purpose: Store sensitive credentials.

Stores
Database Passwords
API Tokens
Certificates
Never Store In
application.yml
Dockerfile
GitHub

10. ECS Auto Scaling

Purpose: Auto-scale Tasks.

Example
CPU > 70%

2 Tasks
   ↓
10 Tasks

Configured Using
CloudWatch Alarms
Target Tracking
🏆 Most Asked ECS Task Definition
{
  "family": "springboot-task",

  "networkMode": "awsvpc",

  "requiresCompatibilities": [
    "FARGATE"
  ],

  "cpu": "512",

  "memory": "1024",

  "containerDefinitions": [
    {
      "name": "springboot-app",

      "image": "ecr-url/springboot:latest",

      "portMappings": [
        {
          "containerPort": 8080
        }
      ],

      "environment": [
        {
          "name": "SPRING_PROFILES_ACTIVE",
          "value": "prod"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

